From fe2cdeb0ea256724bb80df20544601a33828fb6b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bare <git@barebrowser.org>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 17:30:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Register twelve fewer components with update.googleapis.com

Every registration announces the install to update.googleapis.com and asks
for data, carrying a component id, a version, an install date, a freshness
value and a cohort. That is a fair price for something the browser uses and
no price at all for something it does not.

Dropped: SubresourceFilter, because Safe Browsing is what marks a site
abusive and this build has no handler, so nothing can trigger the filter, and
uBlock Origin ships here regardless. OnDeviceHeadSuggest, a Google-built
omnibox model. OptimizationHints, a per-page hint feed and the chattiest of
the set. Trust tokens, private verification tokens, First-Party Sets and the
Privacy Sandbox attestations, all Sandbox plumbing, and without attestations
the Sandbox APIs stay off, which is the wanted answer. HistorySearchStrings,
which feeds on-device AI history search this build does not offer.
MediaEngagementPreload, which seeds autoplay from data Google aggregated,
where local engagement still accrues from the users own browsing.
RealTimeUrlChecksAllowlist, an allowlist for Safe Browsing checks that never
run. CommerceHeuristics and AmountExtractionHeuristicRegexes, shopping and
checkout-amount parsing for features that are not present.

Kept on purpose, because contacting Google is not the same as being useless:
CRLSet for certificate revocation, PKIMetadata for Certificate Transparency,
SSLErrorAssistant for interstitial quality, FileTypePolicies for download
classification, OriginTrials for web compatibility, Widevine for DRM, and
SafetyTips and CrowdDeny, which warn about lookalike domains and abusive
notification prompts from a downloaded list without reporting what is
visited.

ActorSafetyLists, Indigo and CaptchaProvider are left registered. They are
new and their purpose is not clear enough from the tree to remove them
confidently.

DeleteHistorySearchStringsComponent still runs, so its two headers stay.
